#5210
Sloping Hills~
   You wander in some tall grass, just east of the site of a tectonic shift,
where plates far below you have pushed masses of granite and basalt to the
surface to form an effective barrier against travel. The reeds below your
feet crunch with dryness and you realize that even a single bolt of lightning
could set the fields alight.
   The hills continue all around you, growing steeper as you head south.
