#5233
A Carved Cliff~
   You stand below a vertical cliff, looking out over the northern horizon,
across fields and rolling hills of tall grass. Here, someone has taken the
time to chisel into the rock the head of a serpent - a companion to the one
across the road to the east. It appears that gems or glass were once in place
in the carving's eyes, but have long since vanished.
   The hills continue to the west and north, while a road appears to scale the
mountains to the east. Only the cliff face appears to the south, and there
seems no way to scale it.
~
