#5264
A Mountain Road~
   You stand on a steep road, surrounded by tall pines that block the rushing
winds whipping their green tops. The view from here is extraordinary, and to
the north you can look out and see the desert and the ocean beyond. Mossy
rocks rest to either side of the road, the grooves at their bases showing
signs that they had been moved from the ascending trail to allow easier passage
up and down the mountain.
   The road descends into the lower elevations to the north, and climbs high
into the clouds to the south. Rocks and trees lie too dense to travel anywhere
except to the east.
~
