#5284
A Mountainous Trail~
   You stand on a rock-strewn road that ascends the icy mountain above. The
air is thin here, and you find yourself taking two deep breaths just to keep
your vision from becoming blurred and your head from swimming. The air smells
of rich pine, and its heady scent is only reinforced by the jumbles of pine
cones that litter both the steep road and the forest flanking it.
   The road ascends the mountain to the south, and slopes downward to the
north.
~
