#5294
A Mountain Pass~
   You stand at a gusty, snowy mountain pass. A narrow road cuts through a
break in the peak before you to the south, slicing through a large jumble of
fallen stones that flank the open road. The way south seems to level off a bit
into a plateau-like smoothness into the peaks before turning steeply upward
after a few hundred yards, while the road bends sharply down the face of the
mountain to the north.
~
